# Feature: metadata on the original file (Phase 4)

`python/core/metadata.py` writes classification tags onto the **original file**. Analysis 16 kHz audio is never written next to it.

## Formats

- **WAV / AIFF / MP3:** mutagen ID3. `TXXX` desc=`Fieldy`, text = ordered unique class names. `TXXX` desc=`FieldyScore`. `COMM` desc=`Fieldy`, lang=`eng`.
- **FLAC:** Vorbis comments `Fieldy` / `FieldyScore` (keys are case-insensitive on read). Comment field holds the same names.
- `read_tags(path)` returns the Fieldy name list. Untagged file → `[]`.
- Re-tagging replaces previous Fieldy frames and leftover `SoundlyLite` frames.
- `read_tags` still accepts the old `SoundlyLite` descriptor so existing library files keep their tags.

## Invariants

- Samples stay the same container/codec; tagging must not transcode. WAV 32-bit float tests hash PCM via `soundfile.read`. MP3 compare uses a looser tolerance.
- Tag **before** `shutil.move` in ingest (`python/core/ingest.py`). Copy mode tags the library copy after `copy2`, not the source.

## Tests

`python/tests/test_metadata.py`: WAVE round-trip including commas; replace tags; empty read; PCM checksum; legacy `SoundlyLite`; FLAC/AIFF/MP3 round-trip.
